.TH UNIM-GUI-GTK 1 "April 2026" "UNIM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-gui\-gtk \- UNIM tray indicator and settings dialog (GTK4/libadwaita)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-gui\-gtk
.RI [ \-\-settings ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-gui\-gtk
is the user-facing GUI companion of the UNIM input method engine. It
provides:
.IP \(bu 2
A system tray indicator showing the current input mode (Korean/English)
and acting as a quick-toggle.
.IP \(bu 2
The Hanja conversion popup window.
.IP \(bu 2
The special-character / emoji search popup.
.IP \(bu 2
A libadwaita-based settings dialog covering layouts, toggle keys,
TypeFix behaviour, per-application rules and GNOME Shell integration.
.PP
The program is normally launched automatically by
.B /etc/xdg/autostart/unim\-gui\-gtk.desktop
on session start. It communicates with
.B unim\-daemon
over the
.B org.atit.unim.InputMethod
D-Bus session interface; if the daemon is not running it is started on
demand via D-Bus activation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the settings dialog directly instead of starting the tray
indicator. Used by the GNOME Shell extension to redirect "Preferences".
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/xdg/autostart/unim\-gui\-gtk.desktop
Autostart entry installed by the package.
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
Configuration file shared with
.BR unim\-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-config (1),
.BR unim\-gui\-qt (1)
